# Soundappan!

This man from Kumarapalayam near Bhavani was brutally attacked in Thyagaraya Nagar on the eighteenth and lay unconscious. His fingers were torn, his skull fractured, and the bone in his arm broken. So savagely did the arrows of "Acharya" strike him with their sticks.

The comrade had gone to participate in the picketing and is the proprietor of a handloom-cloth shop in Madras. The police officers not only allowed him to be attacked but did not even lift him as he lay like a corpse.

During testimony in the "case of the five," a police officer named Sundaram admitted this.

Not only was the injured man denied treatment; a police officer went to his bed in Royapettah Hospital and arrested him there.

One shudders upon seeing Comrade Soundappan. So many blows! Alas, is this Rama Rajya? Is this what is called self-rule?

(*Dravida Nadu*, 9 August 1953)
